#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Standalone momentum trading agent backtester -- self-contained, no network,
no API keys, no external dependencies (pure Python 3 standard library only).

This is a portable extract of a larger 9-agent momentum/engulfing-pattern
trading system. It embeds REAL market data for XAUUSD (spot gold) pulled
via an Interactive Brokers MCP connector's get_price_history call:
  - 90 real daily closes (used for RSI/MACD/SMA indicator entries)
  - 700 real 1-hour OHLC bars (used for engulfing-pattern entries)
No prices in this file are synthetic or randomly generated.

Architecture (same as the full system):
  9 "agents" feed a weighted-average decision: Technical Analyst carries
  50% of the vote, the other averaged agents (Fundamental/Sentiment/News/
  Bull/Bear/Geopolitical) share the remaining 50%. Macro is a DAMPENER,
  excluded from the average and applied afterward as a multiplicative
  factor / hard suppress-buy override. Geopolitical carries a crisis
  override (rating <= 1.5 caps the decision at HOLD).

  Since this standalone script has no live API keys or network access,
  every agent except Technical Analyst and Macro (whose FOMC-proximity
  signal is pure local calendar math, no API needed) reports a neutral
  rating (3) with confidence 0.0 and data_source='degraded_no_data' --
  exactly what the full system does when those feeds are unreachable.
  Nothing here is faked as "real" when it isn't.

  Entry mode is set by ENTRY_MODE below:
    'indicator' -- daily RSI > 65, MACD positive divergence, price > SMA20
    'engulfing' -- 5-min/1-hour bullish/bearish candlestick engulfing
                   patterns (real 1-hour bars embedded below), gated
                   through the same 9-agent pipeline before a BUY fires

  Exit logic (checked in this order, every day): stop_loss (-2%),
  take_profit (+5%), pattern_reversal (engulfing mode: a bearish
  engulfing print against a held long), agent_decision (weighted rating
  flips to SELL), window_close (force-close at the end of the backtest).

Usage: just run it -- `python3 grok_momentum_backtest.py`
Change ENTRY_MODE / INITIAL_CAPITAL / WINDOW_DAYS below to try variants.
"""

import math
from datetime import datetime, timezone, time as dtime

